nwg-displays (0.5.0-0oaxaca1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.5.0: mangowm support (through wlr-randr, used
    only under mangowm) and niri includes with extra properties kept. The
    Python modules nwg-displays imports are those of 0.4.4 plus the
    standard library's re, so the dependencies are unchanged.
  * hyprland-use-given-paths.patch: on Hyprland, nwg-displays creates its
    monitor and workspace files at the -m and -w paths instead of
    ~/.config/hypr/monitors.conf and workspaces.conf, and reads mirrors and
    the workspaces window from those paths. Started by
    @DISTRO_ID@-launch-monitors with ~/.config/hypr/monitors-gui.conf, 0.4.4
    left two empty files under ~/.config/hypr and opened the workspaces
    window empty; 0.5.0 does the same unpatched.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:16:00 -0500

nwg-displays (0.4.4-0oaxaca1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.4, built for @DISTRO_NAME@ from Debian's 0.3.28-1
    packaging (roadmap step 6, the display settings app). Ubuntu's archive has
    0.3.28, which writes only the old monitors.conf format; Hyprland 0.55 and
    newer, and Omarchy v4.0.4 with it, read a Lua configuration, and
    nwg-displays writes ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua (hl.monitor blocks) and
    workspaces.lua next to the .conf files since 0.4.3. 0.4.4 adds Hyprland
    colour management and VRR fields and fixes monitor descriptions that
    contain "#" in the Lua output. 0.4.0 to 0.4.2 added niri support.
  * d/control: @DISTRO_NAME@ as Maintainer, Debian's maintainer as
    XSBC-Original-Maintainer; Vcs fields dropped (they named Debian's tree).
    Dependencies unchanged: the Python modules nwg-displays imports are the
    same in 0.3.28 and 0.4.4.
  * d/gbp.conf, d/salsa-ci.yml: dropped (Debian's workflow files).
  * The upstream tarball comes from the GitHub release tag, as Debian's
    d/watch fetches it; see the "upstream" file next to debian/.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

